{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "The New Waiter", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Let's Meet Jose", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 1, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 5, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Accurately use information about people's backgrounds in a wider variety  of communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Verb + -ing and to + verb", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A gerund is a noun made by adding \"-ing\" to the base form of a verb. You can use a gerund as the subject, the complement, or the object of a sentence.<br/>The infinitive is the base form of a verb - \u201cto + verb\u201d.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A gerund is the -ing form of a verb that acts as a noun. The noun refers to an activity instead of a person or thing.You can use a gerund as the subject, the complement, or the object of a sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/><br/>  Subject of sentence:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Traveling in the winter is very cold!</span><br/><br/>  Complement of sentence:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">My favorite hobbies are swimming and jogging.</span><br/><br/>  Object of sentence:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm excited to start working in your restaurant.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "An infinitive is a verb form that can acts as a noun. It is formed with to + base form of the verb. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <span class=\"italic\">to talk</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to enjoy</span>, <span class=\"italic\">to play</span><br/> You can<span class=\"italic\">not</span> add <span class=\"strong\">s</span>, <span class=\"strong\">es</span>, <span class=\"strong\">ed</span>, or <span class=\"strong\">ing</span> to the end. It is not a verb.", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I wanted <span class=\"strong\">to know</span>  what kind of adjustments I would need <span class=\"strong\">to make</span> to my life here.</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Inseparable Phrasal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " Phrasal verbs consist of a verb and one or more prepositions. They are common, especially in informal spoken English. The meaning of phrasal verbs is often completely different from the meaning of the verb alone.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Separable phrasal verbs consist of two parts. They always require an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Inseparable phrasal verbs are very common. The verb must be directly followed by its preposition or adverb. Otherwise, the meaning of the phrasal verb will be incorrect.<br/>Some inseparable phrasal verbs never use an object.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "  Examples: <ul><li>get up = get out of bed<br/>    <span class=\"italic\">I get up at seven o'clock every morning.</span></li> <li>take off = leave the ground  <br/>         The plane took off on time.</span></li> <li>look out = beware! be careful!   <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Look out! That car is going to hit you!</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the following inseparable phrasal verbs to describe life experiences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Phrasal Verb\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to read up on\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to read information about a subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to keep at\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to continue doing something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to carry on with\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to continue doing something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to make up for\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to compensate for something missing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to see to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" to take care of something\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " <span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: I read up on Boston's winters to prepare myself! <br/>           <span class=\"strong\">  Bob</span>:  Our summers make up for the cold, though. You'll see.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to read up on", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to spend time researching information on something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I read up on Boston's winters to prepare myself.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use in a new work environment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to keep at", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to continue doing something; to persevere", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: You need to understand how the kitchen works before you start working.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: I'll keep at it.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to carry on with ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to continue doing something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need to carry on with today's tasks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to make up for", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to take care of something lost or missed", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Our summers make up for the cold winters.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to see to", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to deal with or take responsibility for someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I need to see to my customers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "work ethic", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a belief in the importance of work to build character", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You seem to have a strong work ethic.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "adjustment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to adapt to a situation or condition", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I wanted to know what kind of adjustments I would need to make to my life here.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le05ob01aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a list of five places you have been in the last few days.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange the list with a partner. Ask and answer the question <span class=\"italic\">Why did you go to ... ?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use infinitives to give your answer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Now, write five sentences about yourself using a gerund.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use adjectives to complete the sentences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Exchange with a partner and discuss.", "type": "tex